# Native dependencies, pinned by content.
#
# liblogosdelivery has no canonical distribution, and building it from source
# takes tens of minutes, so it arrives as a prebuilt binary from a release
# asset (built from source by docker/build-lib.Dockerfile). It is then
# linked into every binary, baked into the published container, installed under
# /opt, and run as root with NET_ADMIN and host networking — and on Android it
# goes inside the VPN app that sees all traffic and holds the network key.
#
# It was fetched over HTTPS with no other check, which trusts whoever can write
# that release: an account compromise, a hostile fork reached through the REPO
# or DEPS_TAG environment overrides, or a mistake in repackaging. TLS proves who
# served the bytes, not what the bytes are.
#
# So each asset is pinned here by sha256 and verified after download. Changing
# the pinned version is deliberately two steps — bump the tag, update the hash —
# because a version bump that silently accepts new native code is the thing this
# file exists to prevent.
#
# Format: <sha256>  <tag>/<asset>
# Verified with: sha256sum -c, after rewriting the path to the download.

